  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>State function:</p><p>It&nbsp;is a property&nbsp;of which value does not depend on the&nbsp;path&nbsp;only depends upon the initial and final point&nbsp;</p><p>Like: Internal energy&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi></mfenced></math>,&nbsp;Gibb&#39;s&nbsp;free energy<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Path function: Does not depend upon the initial and final point like heat energy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and work done&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi></mfenced></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mtext>q</mtext><mo>+</mo><mtext>w</mtext><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mtext>U</mtext><mo>&#8592;</mo><mtext>definite&#8201;quantity</mtext></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></math> Path function<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></math> Path function<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></math>&nbsp;State function.</p><p><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Answer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p>",
